@node Part01 "Introduction To FileIDToolBox by Re/Y\o/TLS/MST "

                              .: Introduction :.
                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Well it is very easy ... FileIDToolBox can be used to make life easier for
the once that want to add the File_ID.Diz to every available archive you
want to release ... It allows you to add, delete, view and change the 
File_ID.Diz in any archive supported by FileIDToolBox ... It is the workbench-
interface of FileIDCLIBox ... It works on itself ... So you don't need the
FileIDCLIBox ...

This release is only because of a few bug fixes ... It wouldn't take the
file_id.diz always ... It had problems with the "Ram Disk:" from the
reqtools-requester and CED ... So I hope that these problems are fixed
now ... It now also deletes the old description if you select "Add" or
"Change" becoz it is required for some Adders ...

@endnode
@node Part02 "Requirements"

                              .: Requirements :.
                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

All you need is an ©Amiga, OS2.x+, FileIDToolBox, a textviewer, a texteditor
and some archivers ...
If you find any BUGS or have some SUGGESTIONS please leave me a messy ... You
will most certainly be able to find me at @{" Diabolo " Link Diabolo}.


@endnode
@node Part03 "How To Install FileIDToolBox by Re/Y\o/TLS/MST"

                            .:Installation Guide:.
                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The Program runs on most amiga configurations ... there shouldn't be much
limitations ... except not enough diskspace ... not enough ram ... but it
doesn't consume much itself ... it's just the archives that might consume
some space ...
Just copy the program where you like it ...

There are a few Safety requesters just before an operation takes place ...
The

                       "Add File_ID.Diz now?"
                      "Change File_ID.Diz now?"

requesters are only there if you use an editor that detaches from shell and 
immediatly returns ... After changing the File_ID.Diz and saving it with your
favourit editor just press yes if you want it to be added ... Doing this before
you edited the File_ID.Diz will result in the same File_ID.Diz added again ...
You can use multiselect to do different files in one time ... doesn't matter
if they are from a different type ... but you have to handle them one by one ...
becoz otherwise every File_ID.Diz will be overwritten by a newer one ... This
means you have to answer the above two questions only after editing ... Then
you the program will continue with the next one ...

I used a lot of @{" ToolTypes " Link ToolTypes} in the FileIDToolBox.info becoz
i think it makes it more configurable to your own needs ... You can use the
same icon for FileIDCLIBox and FileIDToolBox and only have to change them once
with The ToolTypeWindow or with the ToolType program by Michael J Barsoom
© 1993. You just need to copy it from one to the other ...

Just Click And Answer The Questions And You Are Adding, Deleting, Changing and
Viewing Available File_ID.Diz files ...

@endnode
@node ToolTypes "The different ToolTypes"


                          .:The different ToolTypes:.
                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This is how i build them ... First of all I get the extension of the archive,
this is like DMS, LHA, LZH, EXE etc ... default is "" (nothing) for executables.
For executables there is a program EXEDescript that hangs a description on the
executable without destroying it ... It can also be removed ...
Then i add something to this extension ...

* '.A' : this allows you to specify the add line you want to use for this
         extension ...
         e.g. DMS.A=DMSDescript a %f %F
              ZIP.A=ZIP -u %F %f

Note: if you add the File_ID.Diz by requester it's name doesn't have to be
File_ID.Diz ... it can be anything and it will be added as File_ID.Diz ...

* '.E' : this allows you to specify the edit line you want to use for this
         extension ...
         e.g. DMS.E=CED %f
              ZIP.E=CED %f

* '.X' : this allows you to specify the extract line you want to use for this
         extension ...
         e.g. DMS.X=DMSDescript x %f %F
              ZIP.X=UNZIP -o %F %f

* '.D' : this allows you to specify the delete line you want to use for this
         extension ...
         e.g. DMS.D=DMSDescript d %f %F
              ZIP.D=ZIP -d %F %f

* '.V' : this allows you to specify the view line you want to use for this
         extension ...
         e.g. DMS.V=PPMore %f
              ZIP.V=PPMore %f

Then ... what does the %F and %f mean ... %F will be replaced by the archive
name and path itself ... %f will always be replaced by FILE_ID.DIZ ... so they
must be put there if you want something to happen ... and they have to be at
the exact place for your archiver, editor, viewer ...

There should be enough example ToolTypes in the Icon as is .. so there you can
have a look at the possibilities ...

@endnode
